#### <span id="page-406-0"></span>**Remarks**

**HIAI\_DVPP\_DMalloc** is a new API for allocating memory to DVPP. The memory allocated by using this API can meet the various memory requirements of DVPP.

If **HIAI\_DMalloc(1000, buffer, 1000, HIAI\_MEMORY\_HUGE\_PAGE)** is called to allocate memory for DVPP in the earlier version, use **HIAI\_DVPP\_DMalloc** instead. For details, see **[8.2.5.3.1 HIAI\\_DMalloc](#page-402-0)**.

Usage Example:

// Allocate memory by using **HIAI\_DVPP\_DMalloc**. uint32\_t allocSize = 1000; char\* allocBuffer = (char\*)HIAI\_DVPP\_DMalloc(allocSize); if (allocBuffer == nullptr) { // If the allocation fails, handle the exception. }

[Doc: Atlas200AIAcceleratorModuleApplicationSoftwareDevelopmentGuide_Models3000_ > **8.2.5 Auxiliary APIs** > **Calling Example** > <span id="page-413-0"></span>**Remarks**]

#### <span id="page-413-0"></span>**Remarks**

**HIAIMemory::HIAI\_DVPP\_DMalloc** is a new API for allocating memory to DVPP. The memory allocated by using this API can meet the various memory requirements of DVPP.

If **HIAIMemory::HIAI\_DMalloc(1000, buffer, 1000, HIAI\_MEMORY\_HUGE\_PAGE)** is called to allocate memory for DVPP in the earlier version, use **HIAIMemory::HIAI\_DVPP\_DMalloc** instead. For details, see **[8.2.5.4.1](#page-407-0) [HIAIMemory::HIAI\\_DMalloc](#page-407-0)**.

Usage Example:

// Allocate memory by using **HIAI\_DVPP\_DMalloc**. uint32\_t allocSize = 1000; char\* allocBuffer = nullptr; HIAI\_StatusT ret = hiai::HIAIMemory::HIAI\_DVPP\_DMalloc(allocSize, (void\*&)allocBuffer); if (ret != HIAI\_OK || allocBuffer == nullptr) { // If the allocation fails, handle the exception. }

